---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
  title="About CalcTax — Free Canadian Tax Calculators"
  description="CalcTax.ca provides free, privacy-first income tax calculators for Canadians. Learn how our calculations work and where our data comes from."
>
  <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 pt-10 sm:pt-14"><div class="prose">
    <h1>About CalcTax</h1>

    <p>
      CalcTax.ca is a free tax calculator built for Canadians. We provide
      fast, accurate income tax estimates for all 13 provinces and territories
      — with no signup and no data collection.
    </p>

    <h2>Why We Built This</h2>
    <p>
      Most tax calculators online are either behind a signup wall, loaded with
      ads, or send your financial data to a server. We believe Canadians deserve
      a simple tool that respects their privacy. CalcTax runs entirely in your
      browser — your income, deductions, and tax results never leave your device.
    </p>

    <h2>How Our Calculations Work</h2>
    <p>
      Every calculation is performed client-side using JavaScript. We apply the
      same progressive tax bracket math that the CRA uses:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Federal tax across all five brackets, including the 14.5% blended lowest rate for 2025 and 14% from 2026</li>
      <li>Provincial and territorial tax, including Ontario's surtax, health premium, tax reduction and LIFT credit, and the low-income reductions other provinces offer</li>
      <li>Non-refundable credits: the basic personal amount (with the high-income reduction), the Canada employment amount, and credits for CPP/QPP, EI and QPIP</li>
      <li>CPP/QPP contributions, including CPP2, with the enhanced part deducted from income as on a real return</li>
      <li>EI premiums, Quebec's lower EI rate and QPIP</li>
      <li>Quebec's federal abatement and deduction for workers</li>
      <li>Self-employment income: both halves of CPP/QPP and the deduction for the employer half</li>
      <li>Dividend gross-up and tax credits, capital gains at the 50% inclusion rate, and RRSP and FHSA deductions</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Results are checked by an automated test suite against amounts worked out by hand from the CRA and provincial
      tax forms. If you find a number that doesn't match your return, please <a href="/contact">tell us</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Our Data Sources</h2>
    <p>
      All tax rates, brackets, and thresholds are sourced from official publications:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Canada Revenue Agency (CRA)</strong> — federal tax brackets, CPP/EI rates, basic personal amounts</li>
      <li><strong>Provincial finance departments</strong> — provincial tax brackets and credits</li>
      <li><strong>Revenu Qu&eacute;bec</strong> — Quebec-specific rates (QPP, QPIP, provincial brackets)</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Rates are verified against multiple sources and updated for each tax year. Figures for a year that hasn't
      been officially published yet are marked as projected until the CRA and the provinces confirm them. You can
      see every number we use on the <a href="/2026-canadian-tax-data">tax data</a> pages.
    </p>

    <h2>Limitations</h2>
    <p>
      CalcTax provides <strong>estimates only</strong> for a single person under 65 with no dependants. The
      calculators don't include credits such as tuition, medical expenses, donations or amounts for a spouse or
      dependants, or situations like part-year residency. For a complete tax assessment,
      consult a qualified tax professional. See our
      <a href="/disclaimer">full disclaimer</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>How We Earn Revenue</h2>
    <p>
      CalcTax earns revenue through referral and affiliate links. After you use our
      calculators, we may suggest relevant products like tax filing software.
      If you sign up through our link, we may receive a referral bonus or commission at no
      extra cost to you. Affiliate relationships never influence calculator
      results. See our <a href="/disclosure">affiliate disclosure</a> for details.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Have a question, found an error, or interested in partnering with us?
      Reach out at <a href="/contact">our contact page</a>.
    </p>
  </div></div>
</Base>
